{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Not by a mighty hand.</b> Its meaning is: not by one mighty hand, that is, he will not send you by one hand, with one plague, but by many hands, that is, by ten plagues. Or the meaning of ולא is 'except.' And the Sages of blessed memory interpreted: 'not by a mighty hand' means not by his hand — that is, that refusal was not from the side of his power, his mighty hand, but from mine, as it says (Exodus 6:1) ״כי ביד חזקה ישלחם״ — that is, by my mighty hand; and so is the view of Onkelos: 'and not because of his strong fear.' And this is why Scripture juxtaposes to it: ״ושלחתי את ידי והכיתי את מצרים בכל נפלאתי״ — deficient in ו״ו, because it says בכל נפלאותי and it is impossible that all His wonders were present, but only some of them, in the manner of what is written (Job 26:14): ״הן אלה קצות דרכיו ומה שמץ דבר נשמע בו ורעם גבורותיו מי יתבונן״." "<b>And it is possible</b> by way of the Kabbalah: since the plagues of Egypt were ten, corresponding to the count of the ten sefirot, therefore He mentioned בכל נפלאותי — they are an allusion to the totality of the sefirot, for the last one, called כל, is drawn and emanated from the אל\"ף, which is פלא, and likewise it is wondrous and far beyond attainment." "<b>And behold,</b> all the miracles and wonders that were performed from the six days of creation onward — are they not from the power of the hidden אל\"ף? For the celebrated and revealed miracles are found to come from the hidden world. And behold, נפלאתי is deficient in ו״ו because of the intensity of its hiddenness and because of the deficiency of its attainment. And since it is called אל\"ף and it is a hidden thing, the revealed miracles were called נפלאות, because from the hidden thing the revealed is found. Therefore the beginning of emanation and its end are alluded to in these two words, and the measurement of the verse is: ״והכיתי את מצרים״ in the count that includes all my wonders. And this is the reason for the doubling of 'hand' in the verse at the end of the parashah, where it says: ״כי ביד חזקה ישלחם וביד חזקה יגרשם״. And the order of the plagues — דצ\"ך עד\"ש באח\"ב — follows the order of the sefirot from below upward, for blood corresponds to the attribute of Malkhut, and so all of them. And this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:00.129473354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}